  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 7 files that make up Ceph RGW's S3 authentication implementation:\n\n1. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth_s3.h`** / **`src/rgw/rgw_auth_s3.cc`** \u2014 AWS SigV2/SigV4 mechanics: canonical request/header construction, `is_time_skew_ok()` (the replay/timestamp-window check), `get_v4_signature()`/`get_v2_signature()`, chunked-upload signature verification (`AWSv4ComplMulti`/`AWSv4ComplSingle`).\n2. **`src/rgw/rgw_rest_s3.h`** / **`src/rgw/rgw_rest_s3.cc`** \u2014 the REST-layer auth engines (`LocalEngine`, `LDAPEngine`, `STSEngine`, `AWSGeneralAbstractor`) that extract credentials from the request, look up the secret key, and perform the actual signature comparison; also `RGW_Auth_S3::authorize`.\n3. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth.h`** / **`src/rgw/rgw_auth.cc`** \u2014 the generic pluggable auth framework: `Engine`, `Strategy` (engine chaining/fallback control), `IdentityApplier` hierarchy (`LocalApplier`, `RemoteApplier`, `RoleApplier`), `ImplicitTenants`.\n4. **`src/rgw/rgw_auth_registry.h`** \u2014 `StrategyRegistry`, which wires the S3 engines together and defines the V4-plain \u2192 V4-boto2 `SUFFICIENT`/`FALLBACK` ordering (the SigV2/V4 fallback chain of interest for the audit).",
